  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.5.0 — registration validity is now a compile-time error: an abstract or static implementation is DIG0020, and [Singleton<T>] whose class does not implement T is DIG0021 (both were startup ArgumentExceptions). ServiceRegistrarHelper stays public for hand-written registrars; the generator no longer emits it, so RegisterServices() is plain descriptors. Plus two generator fixes: keyed [AlsoAs<T>(\"key\")] views generated code that did not compile (CS1660), and [Inject] on a nullable member kept no nullability — a nullable field produced CS8600 in every consumer build with nullable enabled (a build failure under TreatWarningsAsErrors), while a nullable value type on a partial property emitted the invalid int??. Unkeyed, enumerable and generic-main forwards are unchanged.",
